# What a search of a Mac's home folder never walks into, for ripgrep and fd
# alike: other programs' data and the folders macOS guards. A search that reaches
# one makes macOS ask whether the searcher may read it, again for every build
# of the searcher, so an agent's search of the home folder asked over and over.
# The cloud's folders are here too, since a search reading one downloads
# each file the Mac doesn't hold yet. A search that names one of them, or starts inside one, still
# searches it.
/Library/Containers/
/Library/Group Containers/
/Library/Mobile Documents/
/Library/CloudStorage/
/Desktop/
/Documents/
/Downloads/
